course: dictionary
lesson: 13835
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Jammed is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits. «The door is jammed, so I cannot open it.» Jammed means stuck, so it will not move. The clue is cannot open it.
explain: «The bus was jammed with people.» Here jammed does not mean stuck. It means packed very full. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Packed would fit, but stuck would not.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. «The bus was stuck with people» does not make sense, so you know you have picked the wrong meaning.
fact: Jammed means stuck so it cannot move or work, as in «the drawer is jammed».
fact: Jammed can mean packed very full, as in «the hall was jammed with fans».
fact: Jammed can mean pushed hard into a small space, as in «she jammed her hat on her head».
fact: Jammed can mean hurt by being squashed, as in «I jammed my thumb in the door».
fact: Never put your fingers into a jammed machine, and a jammed fire exit is dangerous.
exercise: «The printer is jammed, so no pages come out.» What does jammed mean here? | Sung loudly | Full of happy people | *Stuck and not working | Very clean
exercise: «The roads were jammed with cars all morning.» What does jammed mean here? | *Packed very full | Played music together | Hurt by being squashed | Stuck in a tight space
exercise: «Ella jammed her finger in the car door.» What happened to her finger? | Painted bright red | Pushed into a bag | *Hurt by being squashed | Lost in the car
test: «Do not put your fingers in a jammed machine.» Why is this a safety rule? | *It could hurt you | It cleans the machine | It is a fun game | It makes the machine go faster
test: «Dad jammed his clothes into the bag.» What does jammed mean here? | Stuck and could not move | Hurt by being squashed | *Pushed hard into a small space | Packed very full
exam: «The lift was jammed with people.» What does jammed mean here? | Stuck and not moving | Pushed into a small space | *Packed very full | Hurt by being squashed
